text My field of view is filled up by the vast night sky.
text It hurts like hell to breathe. Desperate for oxygen, I find myself gasping for air.
text And each time I do, a grating pain spreads through my chest.
text I'm lying sprawled on the ground.
text My clothes and my hair are mud-stained, but I don't care at all.
text The only thing bothering me is the mix of sand and blood starting to dry on my lips.
