text The door to the classroom opens with a rattle.
text The noisy students all fell silent in an instant.
text They're all looking at my face.
text At the blue bruises and Band-Aids stuck all over it.
text Well, of course I'd stand out like that.
text After a moment, I turn my eyes toward them, and they all quickly avert their gaze.
text I don't really care all that much, though.
text At the same time as always, in the same manner as always...
text I leisurely approach my chair and settle myself down.
text @[Tomoya]
text *Yawn*
text I let out a single yawn.
text It's almost noon already.
text This warm spot in the sun is making a nap really tempting.
text Before long, the classroom returns to its previous noisiness.
text A bit later, the class becomes still as death yet again.
text I direct my half-asleep eyes over to the door.
text A guy is standing there, Band-Aids plastered all over his face.
text A strange, blond guy.
text It's Sunohara, without a doubt.
text He hesitates for a bit, seeing the state of the class, but he soon sluggishly comes walking up to me.
text Our eyes meet.
text Sunohara's legs suddenly come to a stop.
text We both glare fixedly at each other.
text We gaze at each other's faces, the faces we wounded ourselves with our own fists. And then...
text I laugh.
text I laugh from the bottom of my heart.
text His face is somehow just too hilarious. It's changed so dramatically from how it used to be.
text I don't even try holding down my laughter as it comes, and continue on laughing.
text For just a moment, Sunohara looks puzzled...
text And then, he laughs in just the same way.
text We both point at each other, and even as it becomes difficult to breathe...
text We continue laughing.
text @[Tomoya]
text S-Sunohara.
text After laughing for a while, I finally wipe away my oncoming tears.
text @[Tomoya]
text H-How about we go grab some lunch?
